{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/posts/structured-output-from-the-chrome-prompt-api-with-json-schema/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1280px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/00711/hero.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.4375%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/fb34c/hero.avif 320w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/646cd/hero.avif 768w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/8b485/hero.avif 1024w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/a73d6/hero.avif 1280w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/a7f9f/hero.avif 1920w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/fb732/hero.avif 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/cb523/hero.webp 320w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/cd067/hero.webp 768w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/53334/hero.webp 1024w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/4b075/hero.webp 1280w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/f3ff0/hero.webp 1920w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/4293a/hero.webp 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/d4f27/hero.png 320w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/778aa/hero.png 768w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/658fc/hero.png 1024w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/26c69/hero.png 1280w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/7d442/hero.png 1920w,\n/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/00711/hero.png 2400w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/dc9f613dfe5ad2875c0b1bf3b8719ee8/26c69/hero.png\"\n            alt=\"hero\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>TL;DR; Pass a JSON Schema as <code class=\"language-text\">responseConstraint</code> to <code class=\"language-text\">session.prompt()</code> and the Prompt API returns JSON you can parse. It is stable on desktop Chrome for the web since Chrome 148. Still validate the result: valid JSON is not the same as correct data. 🎉</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>This is the third post of my series <em>AI on the web in 2026</em>. The <a href=\"/posts/built-in-ai-in-chrome-summarizer-translator-language-detector-in-production/\">previous one</a> covered the task-based APIs; now it's time for the general one.</p>\n<p>The Prompt API gives you a session with the language model that ships with Chrome. That is powerful, and also a bit dangerous for a UI. Models love to be helpful: \"Sure! Here is your answer:\" followed by Markdown, followed by a friendly closing line. Your component wanted a boolean.</p>\n<p>In this article, we'll explore how to constrain the output with JSON Schema, how to validate it, and what the availability looks like at the end of 2026.</p>\n<h2>The Problem with free-text answers</h2>\n<p>Let's say you want to classify a support message into a category and a priority. Asking nicely in the prompt (\"answer only with JSON\") works most of the time. Most of the time is the problem:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">JSON.parse()</code> throws on a trailing sentence or a code fence.</li>\n<li>Field names drift between calls (<code class=\"language-text\">priority</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">Priority</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">urgency</code>).</li>\n<li>Enum values get creative (<code class=\"language-text\">\"kinda urgent\"</code>).</li>\n<li>Every consumer ends up with its own regex clean-up.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Neither is great for something that renders in production.</p>\n<h2>Availability first</h2>\n<p>The status changed a lot over the last year, so let's be precise. According to the Chrome docs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Chrome Extensions</strong>: the Prompt API is available since Chrome 138.</li>\n<li><strong>The web</strong>: it ships on desktop since Chrome 148, after an origin trial that started in Chrome 139. Sampling settings for the web (<code class=\"language-text\">samplingMode</code>) are in a separate origin trial.</li>\n<li>Structured output with <code class=\"language-text\">responseConstraint</code> is available since Chrome 137.</li>\n<li>Platforms: Windows, macOS, Linux and Chromebook Plus. Android and iOS are not supported yet.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Extensions that still declare the old <code class=\"language-text\">\"aiLanguageModelOriginTrial\"</code> permission should remove it; that trial has expired.</p>\n<h2>The Solution: <code class=\"language-text\">responseConstraint</code></h2>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> schema <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'object'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">properties</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">category</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">enum</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'billing'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'bug'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'account'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'other'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">priority</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">enum</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'low'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'medium'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'high'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">summary</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">required</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'category'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'priority'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">'summary'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">additionalProperties</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">false</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">triage</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">message</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token operator\">!</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'LanguageModel'</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> self<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">null</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> options <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">expectedInputs</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'text'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">languages</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'en'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">expectedOutputs</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'text'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">languages</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'en'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> LanguageModel<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">availability</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>options<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">===</span> <span class=\"token string\">'unavailable'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">null</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> session <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> LanguageModel<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">create</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">...</span>options<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">initialPrompts</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">role</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'system'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">content</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'You triage customer support messages.'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> raw <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> session<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">prompt</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>message<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">responseConstraint</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> schema <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token constant\">JSON</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">parse</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>raw<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">finally</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    session<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">destroy</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, the schema goes in the second argument of <code class=\"language-text\">prompt()</code> (it also works with <code class=\"language-text\">promptStreaming()</code>). The model is constrained to produce JSON that follows it, so <code class=\"language-text\">JSON.parse()</code> is safe and the enums stop drifting.</p>\n<p>Keep in mind that <code class=\"language-text\">availability()</code> takes the same options you will use later. That's how Chrome tells you whether the languages and input types you need are supported on this device.</p>\n<h4>Saving context window</h4>\n<p>By default, the schema is sent to the model as part of the input, which uses context. When your prompt already describes the format, you can skip that:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> session<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">prompt</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>message<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">responseConstraint</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> schema<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">omitResponseConstraintInput</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">true</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>If you do that, describe the expected shape in the prompt itself, otherwise the model has less guidance. You can watch the budget with <code class=\"language-text\">session.contextUsage</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">session.contextWindow</code>.</p>\n<h2>Validate anyway</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Structured output gives you valid JSON. It doesn't give you true JSON.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The Chrome docs recommend testing your schemas and validating outputs. A constrained model can still pick <code class=\"language-text\">\"low\"</code> for a message that says the whole checkout is down. So I add two layers:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Schema validation</strong> at the boundary, with the same schema object. With Ajv, that is <code class=\"language-text\">const validate = new Ajv().compile(schema)</code> and then <code class=\"language-text\">validate(result)</code>. If it fails, treat it as \"no answer\".</li>\n<li><strong>Business rules</strong> that the schema can't express. For example, anything mentioning payments never gets <code class=\"language-text\">low</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> result <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token function\">triage</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>text<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token operator\">!</span>result <span class=\"token operator\">||</span> <span class=\"token operator\">!</span><span class=\"token function\">validate</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>result<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">category</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'other'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">priority</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'medium'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">summary</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">''</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// safe default</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The schema also becomes a contract you can share with the cloud path. If the device can't run the model, the same schema works as <code class=\"language-text\">responseSchema</code> in Gemini, and that is exactly what <a href=\"/posts/hybrid-inference-with-firebase-ai-logic-on-device-first-cloud-fallback/\">hybrid inference with Firebase AI Logic</a> does for you.</p>\n<h2>A few limits worth knowing</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep schemas small.</strong> The examples in the docs use <code class=\"language-text\">type</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">properties</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">items</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">required</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">maxItems</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">additionalProperties</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">pattern</code>. The docs don't list every supported keyword, so test anything more exotic before relying on it.</li>\n<li><strong>First use downloads the model.</strong> When <code class=\"language-text\">availability()</code> returns <code class=\"language-text\">downloadable</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">downloading</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">create()</code> starts the download and needs a user gesture.</li>\n<li><strong>Sessions hold state.</strong> Reuse a session for related prompts, use <code class=\"language-text\">session.clone()</code> to branch, and call <code class=\"language-text\">destroy()</code> when you're done to free resources.</li>\n<li><strong>Text out only.</strong> The API accepts text, image and audio input, but the output is text. JSON is text, so we are fine.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you're building forms on top of this, <a href=\"/posts/signal-forms-and-gemini-ai-assisted-form-filling-that-still-validates/\">Signal Forms and Gemini</a> shows the same \"constrain, then validate\" idea in Angular.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/prompt-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">The Prompt API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/structured-output-for-prompt-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Structured output for the Prompt API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/built-in-apis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Built-in AI APIs overview</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/iR6R7-nQeHI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Intent to Ship: Prompt API (blink-dev)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://ajv.js.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Ajv JSON schema validator</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>That’s all for now</h3>\n<p>Constrain the output, validate the result, and keep a safe default. That's the whole recipe.</p>\n<p>I hope you enjoyed this reading as much as I enjoyed writing it. Thank you so much for reading until the end and see you soon!</p>\n<p>🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Cya 👋</h3>","frontmatter":{"date":"November 23, 2026","path":"/posts/structured-output-from-the-chrome-prompt-api-with-json-schema/","title":"Structured output from the Chrome Prompt API with JSON Schema","tags":["frontend","javascript","ai","chrome","gemini","web"],"status":"active"},"timeToRead":4}},"pageContext":{"postPath":"/posts/structured-output-from-the-chrome-prompt-api-with-json-schema/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1271460761","63159454"],"slicesMap":{}}